Aston Villa, as a [[Premier League]] team not involved in European competition, started in the second round where they played [[EFL League Two]] club [[Crewe Alexandra F.C.|Crewe Alexandra]] away. At [[Gresty Road]], Aston Villa won 6–1 with two goals from [[Conor Hourihane]] as well as goals from [[Ezri Konsa]], [[Keinan Davis]], [[Frederic Guilbert]] and [[Jack Grealish]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49403071 |title=Carabao Cup: Crewe 1-6 Aston Villa |publisher=BBC Sport |date=27 August 2019 |access-date=28 January 2020 |archive-date=2 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210102145411/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49403071 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the third round, they played fellow Premier League side [[Brighton & Hove Albion F.C.|Brighton & Hove Albion]] away at the [[Falmer Stadium]]. Villa won 3–1 with goals from [[Jota (Spanish footballer)|Jota]], Hourihane and Grealish.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49736853 |title=Brighton & Hove Albion 1-3 Aston Villa: Conor Hourihane scores win |publisher=BBC Sport |date=25 September 2019 |access-date=28 January 2020 |archive-date=26 September 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190926001020/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49736853 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the next round, they drew Premier League team [[Wolverhampton Wanderers F.C.|Wolverhampton Wanderers]] at home. At [[Villa Park]], they progressed to the next round with a 2–1 win thanks to goals from [[Anwar El Ghazi]] and [[Ahmed Elmohamady]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Sutcliffe |first=Steve |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50148248 |title=Aston Villa 2-1 Wolverhampton Wanderers |publisher=BBC Sport |date=30 October 2019 |access-date=28 January 2020 |archive-date=31 October 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191031162516/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50148248 |url-status=live }}</ref> 

In the quarter-finals they played Premier League side and European champions [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] at Villa Park. Due to Liverpool's participation in the [[2019 FIFA Club World Cup]] in Qatar soon after, they fielded an inexperienced team and the club's youngest ever starting lineup, while Villa made 10 changes while still fielding mostly senior players.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2019/dec/17/aston-villa-liverpool-carabao-cup-match-report |title=
Aston Villa's Jonathan Kodjia shows no mercy to knock out Liverpool's kids |work=The Guardian |date=17 December 2019 |access-date=22 January 2022}}</ref> Villa won 5–0 with goals from Hourihane, two from [[Jonathan Kodjia]], [[Wesley Moraes|Wesley]] and an [[own goal]] from [[Morgan Boyes]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Stone |first=Simon |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50723225 |title=Aston Villa 5-0 Liverpool: Dean Smith's side overwhelm young Liverpool side |publisher=BBC Sport |date=17 December 2019 |access-date=28 January 2020 |archive-date=21 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191221161840/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50723225 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the two-legged semi-final they played Premier League side [[Leicester City F.C.|Leicester City]]. After a 1–1 draw in the first leg away at the [[King Power Stadium]],<ref>{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50962651 |title=Carabao Cup - Leicester City 1-1 Aston Villa: Kelechi Iheanacho equaliser sets up second leg |publisher=BBC Sport |date=8 January 2020 |access-date=28 January 2020 |archive-date=29 January 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200129212405/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50962651 |url-status=live }}</ref> Villa reached the final after a 2–1 win at Villa Park with goals from [[Matt Targett (footballer)|Matt Targett]] and a 93rd-minute winner from [[Trézéguet (Egyptian footballer)|Trézéguet]] to complete a 3–2 aggregate victory.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/50987790 |title=Aston Villa v Leicester City latest - Carabao Cup semi-final, second leg |publisher=BBC Sport |date=28 January 2020 |access-date=28 January 2020 |archive-date=28 January 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200128213805/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/50987790 |url-status=live }}</ref>

